overview='''<div class="callout"><strong>Newly approved:</strong> coin-value tally → SOLE; HRAFN → five perches → 2648. <a href="#approved">See the full specifications and postcard changes →</a></div><div class="callout alert"><strong>Verdict: strong concept; not yet ready for an unattended full run.</strong> The main problems are missing instructions, unbuilt physical mechanisms and release logistics. These should be fixed before making the puzzles harder.</div>
<div class="statrow card"><div><span class="metric">2–4</span>players, ages 16+</div><div><span class="metric">60–90</span>minute target, not a measured duration</div><div><span class="metric">22</span>existing postcards: 18 route stops + 4 decoys</div><div><span class="metric">11</span>proposed required puzzle gates</div></div>
<div class="grid">'''+panel('What works','<ul><li>Cards repeatedly unlock new meanings: local clue first, route point later.</li><li>Distinct actions: spotting, matching, light alignment, mapping, coin tallying, cipher and board planning.</li><li>The museum tickets give ordinary-looking props a useful role.</li><li>The final invitation pays off Liv’s opening message.</li></ul>')+panel('What must change','<ul><li>Build the coin tally and perch card; prove the light puzzles.</li><li>Fix the extra E-column rune and state the board’s house rules.</li><li>Assign contents and separate locks to every required gate.</li><li>Replace the outdated hints and test the four drawn digits blind.</li></ul>')+'''</div>
<h3 style="margin-top:26px">Answers to the review questions</h3>'''+table(['Question','Assessment'],[
('Do clues and locks make sense?','Most intended transformations do. The original rune selection and board instructions are not fair as printed; the tally props and comb/ruler chains are unfinished. See the detailed audit.'),
('Too easy or too difficult?','The opening should stay easy. Counting and MEAD provide relief. Aud, board reconstruction and the finale are the heavy tasks. Missing rules make several steps feel harder than their actual deductions.'),
('Does it flow?','There is no complete current release plan. The proposed flow closes that gap, corrects runes-before-board, keeps H6 late, and adds parallel work in Rollo and Harald.'),
('Playable by 2–4, ages 16+?','The content and intended reasoning fit this audience without prior Norse knowledge. Conditional yes after fixes and physical proof. Four players need parallel tasks and enough table space; two should be able to progress without a specialist.'),
('Can it fit 60–90 minutes?','Plausible design target after removing the unfinished comb/ruler gates and reducing rule ambiguity. No measured team times exist, so this review cannot certify the duration.')])+'''
<div class="callout"><strong>Recommended scope:</strong> keep 11 required gates. Make the ruler rebus optional; defer the comb lock. This deliberately relaxes “every card must gate a lock”: R3/R4/R5 and AD still matter to the final map puzzle. The original 13-gate plan remains available in the puzzle audit.</div>
<p><a href="#flow">Start with Adventure flow →</a> &nbsp; <a href="#puzzles">Read all findings →</a> &nbsp; <a href="#props">Prepare the props →</a></p>
<details><summary>How this review was done and what it cannot prove</summary><div><p>Read the original brainstorm’s story, systems, puzzle data, final-riddle evidence model, open issues, prop specs and design guide. Checked the recent handoff and clean repository at commit <code>688ed06</code>. Extracted text from the current canonical PDFs and rendered 69 pages, including all 44 postcard sides, the four print maps, their answer maps, tickets and journal. Inspected overview sheets and enlarged critical details. Read relevant builders to resolve contradictions.</p><p>Re-ran the final ordering enumerator; independently searched the fixed 11×11 board and tested the journal’s weaker before/after interpretation. Aud’s 521 is a source-recorded tally, not a new paper-playtest result. Print stock, real light transmission, coin selection/display, lock hardware, container fit, cold solves and unaided shape recognition remain untested. Historical claims were not comprehensively re-researched; historical notes below are internal consistency observations.</p><p>The user confirmed some 3-digit, 4-digit and 4-letter locks, with quantities unknown. Other ownership remains unknown. G7’s coin tally and G8’s five-perch conversion are now approved; other review proposals retain their status. Original production documents and PDFs are untouched.</p></div></details>
'''

flow='''<div class="callout"><strong>Proposed packing plan, not current production status.</strong> Start together → parallel Rollo → Aud together → parallel Harald → shared finale. G7/G8 reflect the approved replacements. Existing incomplete mechanisms must pass the tests before this sequence is runnable.</div><div class="routeband"><span>Leif · learn the language</span><span>Rollo · divide the work</span><span>Aud · tactile discovery</span><span>Harald · two branches</span><span>Finale · reunite</span></div>
<div class="flow">'''
for sid,title,inputs,action,gate,releases,team in FLOW:
    flow+=f'<article class="card stage" id="flow-{sid}"><span class="pill">{sid}</span><h3>{title}</h3><div class="split"><dl><dt>Have in hand</dt><dd>{inputs}</dd><dt>Do / solve</dt><dd>{action}</dd></dl><dl><dt>Opens</dt><dd>{gate}</dd><dt>Find inside</dt><dd>{releases}</dd></dl></div><p class="notice">Team use: {team}</p></article>'
flow+='''</div><h3>Prevent accidental bypasses and dead ends</h3><ul><li>The Rollo pouch must genuinely require both its locks: one closure/hasp needing both to open, not two independent zippers that expose the same contents.</li><li>G8 is a four-digit lock set to 2648 directly on the board-kit pouch. Pack the perch card outside it, in G7; no cryptex or intermediate key is required.</li><li>The MEAD wallet contains the journal; the 253 sleeve contains H6 and the transition tickets. Both branches are needed for the intended finale.</li><li>All released cards and maps remain available. Do not lock a needed tool behind the puzzle it solves.</li><li>Label hint topics and containers by subject (beasts, coin cache, board), with a visible association. Use S/G numbers only for setup; they need not appear in the fiction.</li><li>The original leg-release order already suggests Leif–Rollo–Aud–Harald. Do not claim the final digit order is unknowable before the bundle; tickets should confirm it. Accept a well-reasoned early guess rather than redesigning the whole game to police it.</li></ul>
<h3>Planning time budget</h3><p class="small">These are allocated targets for a future test, not predictions or observed times. Parallel stages use elapsed team time.</p>'''+table(['Stage','Target window','What to watch'],[
('Leif: 3 gates','10–15 min','If two-paper alignment dominates, fix the prop.'),('Rollo: 2 parallel gates','10–15 min','Word operation must be understood; count details readable.'),('Aud: 2 gates','15–20 min','Mapping should be thought, not arguing about crossings.'),('Harald: 3 gates','15–20 min','Rune + MEAD parallel, then board; avoid copying 23 pieces becoming busywork.'),('Finale + reveal','15–20 min','Divide the maps, then combine; no unexplained geography knowledge.'),('Total target','65–90 min','60 minutes is a stretch for first-time teams. Measure before advertising.')])+'''
<h3>Every postcard’s first release</h3>'''+table(['Card','First available','Role'],[(k,v,('Decoy for drawing; retain for earlier clues and travel evidence' if k.endswith('D') else 'Route stop; puzzle roles in the audit')) for k,v in RELEASES.items()])+'''
<details><summary>If you keep all 13 original gates</summary><div><p>Ruler distance and BOOK would each need a defined answer, separate lock, contents and successful physical proof. A serial version increases waiting and reading overhead; its duration is unknown. Do not add either back until the 11-gate pilot is within the desired time. To insert BOOK, release AD + working comb after SOLE and put Harald’s initial packet behind a separate BOOK lock. To insert the ruler gate, place R3/R4/R5 + calibrated ruler after the Rollo join, then place Aud’s packet behind that new numeric lock. These are alternatives, not the recommended first test.</p></div></details>'''

findings='<div class="toolbar"><label for="audit-search">Find a topic</label><input id="audit-search" type="search" placeholder="Try runes, tally, perches, print…"><select id="severity" aria-label="Finding priority"><option value="">All findings</option><option>Blocker</option><option>Fix before testing</option><option>Test risk</option><option>Documentation</option><option>Production gap</option><option>Approved change</option></select></div><p class="small">Stable review IDs RV-01–RV-21. RV-20/RV-21 record the approved replacements. Existing project IDs are retained beside them. “Blocker” means a complete self-guided run cannot yet be relied on.</p>'
