decisions+='<h3>Ready-made proposals in this review</h3><p>Rune-map correction, alternative journal, player-only Aud ticket, six cue slips, the 11-gate release plan and revised hint page are provided for comparison. G7’s value tally and G8’s five-perch conversion have since been approved. Other proposals remain unapproved unless separately recorded. The old balance cue is superseded; production readiness still requires proof.</p><h3>Lower-priority cleanup after playability</h3><ul><li>H1’s printed Fun Fact mentions a 2026 discovery while the current travel itinerary ends in 2025. Either frame these as later editions of her cards or remove the time conflict in a future copy edit. This is an internal date inconsistency, not an independent fact-check of that discovery.</li><li>L3’s front/postmark says Baffin Island while the ticket uses Qikiqtarjuaq; the Leif map pairs Qikiqtarjuaq with the Helluland/Baffin region. Test whether this lookup is clear; a small subtitle would be fairer if players hesitate.</li><li>The guide’s “unmailed cards” premise sits awkwardly with cancelled stamps; keep the collection aesthetic unless it misleads players.</li><li>H2’s image credit renders its Cyrillic author name as missing glyph boxes. Use a Unicode-capable credit font in a later print cleanup.</li><li>Design-only references such as “see stops.js” and “see PZ-17” appear in some player-card credits. Move implementation references into the credits reference page when revising those cards; preserve required attribution.</li></ul>'

design='''<div class="grid">'''+panel('Keep the visual identity','<p>Forest green <code>#283B34</code>, paper <code>#EFE3C4</code>, muted rust <code>#B56A2A</code>. Trail accents: Leif blue, Rollo rust, Aud purple, Harald green. Vintage travel fronts; Liv’s handwriting for messages; typed Fun Facts and ticket furniture.</p>')+panel('Make instructions easier to find','<p>Give task/rule text breathing room. Keep the small family mark separate from rebus drawings. Keep stamp motifs and written place names useful without colour. A new player should distinguish a puzzle instruction from decorative history without reading designer notes.</p>')+panel('Preserve the challenge','<p>Explain operations when otherwise arbitrary: count movement not endpoints, move only the king, retain discarded-route cards, sum selected coin values, follow direct perch connections, keep north up. The deduction is which data to combine, not guessing the designer’s unstated convention.</p>')+panel('Type and physical usability','<p>5×3.5-inch cards are compact for four people. Give one reader space to read aloud; use the larger journal proposal. Proof labels and credits at actual size. Magnification should support close-looking puzzles, not rescue all reading. Ensure final map marks can be wiped without damaging paper.</p>')+'''</div><h3 style="margin-top:24px">How the review page is organized</h3><p>Overview for verdict; Adventure flow for packing; Puzzle audit for mechanism and evidence; Props checklist for production; Gallery for comparing art; Playtest & hints for verification; Decisions for unresolved choices. Old explanations remain accessible in the base brainstorm instead of appearing next to current instructions.</p><p>'''+ref('guide','Open the complete original design guide')+' · '+ref('options','Open original parked ideas')+'</p>'

